<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4865" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμαιμάκετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Hes.
			<u>Sc.</u>
			207
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>irresistible,</i> old 
				Ep.
			 word, also in Lyr. and Trag. (lyr.); of Chimaera, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.179
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16.329
			</span></i>; of fire vomited by her, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				319
			</span></i>; of fire generally, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				177
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλασσα, πόντος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				207
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.14
			</span></i>; of ship's mast, proof against any strain, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.311
			</span></i>; of the trident, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				8(7).37
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μένος, κινηθμός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				3.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.208
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεῖκος</span>”
				<i>stubborn,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					10.64
				</span></i>
			; of the Furies, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				127
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. βυθοῖς</span> in
				<i>unfathomable</i> depths, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.900
			</span></i>. [Usu. derived fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ</span>-
			intens., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαιμάω,</span> i. e.
			<i>furious;</i> but apptly. connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμαχος</span> by Poets.]</div>
